<Rechtstext titel="Privacy policy" pfad="/en/privacy" beschreibung="How Horoskop-Geschenk.de handles your data, what birth details are used for and when they are deleted.">
  <p class="nebentext">Last updated: {anbieter.stand.en}</p>

  <h2>In short</h2>
  <p>
    We only collect what we need for your horoscope: first name, date of birth, time of birth, place of birth and your
    email address. We use no tracking cookies, create no customer account and do not pass your data on for
    advertising. We delete the birth details 30 days after delivery.
  </p>

  <h2>Controller</h2>
  <Anbieter lang="en" />

  <h2>What data we process and why</h2>

  <h3>Ordering and creating the horoscope</h3>
  <p>
    For the order we process the details of the person the horoscope is for (first name, date of birth, time of birth
    or the note that it is unknown, place of birth with coordinates and time zone), the chosen edition and your email
    address. We use them to calculate, create and send the horoscope. The legal basis is the performance of the
    contract (Art. 6 (1) (b) GDPR).
  </p>
  <p>
    Birth details are not special categories of personal data within the meaning of Art. 9 GDPR. We nevertheless treat
    them with particular care: they are used only for your horoscope, not analysed and not passed on, except to the
    service providers named below where this is necessary for creation.
  </p>

  <h3>Horoscopes as a gift</h3>
  <p>
    If you give a horoscope as a gift, you enter another person’s details. We process them solely to create the gift.
    The legal basis is our and your legitimate interest in carrying out the gift order (Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR). The
    recipient can contact us at any time and has the same rights as you.
  </p>

  <h3>Creating the texts</h3>
  <p>
    To create the texts we use a technical service provider that works on our behalf and on our instructions (data
    processing under Art. 28 GDPR). For this we transmit the calculated astrological positions and, where applicable,
    the first name, but no email address and no payment data. The service provider may use the data only for this
    purpose. <span class="platzhalter">[Place of processing: “Processing takes place in the EU.” or “Data may be transferred to the USA; the basis is the European Commission’s adequacy decision (EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework) or standard contractual clauses.”]</span> The legal basis is Art. 6 (1) (b) GDPR. On request, we will tell you the name of the service
    provider.
  </p>

  <h3>Payment</h3>
  <p>
    Payment is handled by Stripe (Stripe Payments Europe, Ltd., 1 Grand Canal Street Lower, Dublin 2, Ireland). Stripe
    processes your name, payment details and email address under its own responsibility to process the payment and
    prevent fraud. We never see card details. Stripe may also transfer data to the USA; the European Commission’s
    adequacy decision (EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework) and standard contractual clauses apply. The legal basis is
    Art. 6 (1) (b) GDPR. More in Stripe’s privacy policy at stripe.com/privacy.
  </p>

  <h3>Sending emails</h3>
  <p>
    We send the order confirmation and the horoscope via an email service provider working on our behalf (Art. 28
    GDPR). It processes your email address and the content of the message. <span class="platzhalter">[Place of processing: “Processing takes place in the EU.” or “Data may be transferred to the USA; the basis is the European Commission’s adequacy decision (EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework) or standard contractual clauses.”]</span> The legal basis is Art. 6 (1) (b)
    GDPR.
  </p>

  <h3>Hosting and server log files</h3>
  <p>
    The website is hosted by a hosting service provider working on our behalf (Art. 28 GDPR). <span class="platzhalter">[Place of processing: “Processing takes place in the EU.” or “Data may be transferred to the USA; the basis is the European Commission’s adequacy decision (EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework) or standard contractual clauses.”]</span> When a page is accessed, the server processes technically necessary data such as IP
    address, time, requested address and browser identifier in order to deliver the page and protect it against
    attacks. The legal basis is our legitimate interest in secure operation (Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR). Log data is deleted
    after no more than <span class="platzhalter">[number]</span> days.
  </p>

  <h3>Place suggestions in the order form</h3>
  <p>
    So that you do not have to spell the place of birth exactly, the form suggests places. For this, the place name
    you type is transmitted together with your IP address to the geocoding service of Open-Meteo (Switzerland). The
    European Commission has adopted an adequacy decision for Switzerland. The legal basis is Art. 6 (1) (b) GDPR,
    because the exact place is necessary for the calculation.
  </p>

  <h3>Storage in the browser</h3>
  <p>
    We do not set cookies. The site stores in the browser only what it needs to work: the chosen light or dark view for
    the duration of the visit, and the cart with the birth details entered. The cart stays on your device until you
    order and is deleted automatically after three days without an order. The legal basis is section 25 (2) no. 2
    TDDDG (German Telecommunications Digital Services Data Protection Act), because this storage is strictly necessary
    for the service you requested.
  </p>

  <h3>Fonts and audience measurement</h3>
  <p>
    All fonts are hosted on our own server; no data is transmitted to Google or other font providers.
    <span class="platzhalter">[If Plausible is used: We count visits with Plausible Analytics (Plausible Insights OÜ,
    Estonia), without cookies and without personal reference. Legal basis Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR. Otherwise delete this
    paragraph.]</span>
  </p>

  <h3>News by email</h3>
  <p>
    If you tick the box for news when ordering, we occasionally send you an email about new offers and vouchers. The
    box is voluntary and not required for the order. So that nobody can enter someone else’s address, you confirm the
    sign-up via a link in a first email. The legal basis is your consent (Art. 6 (1) (a) GDPR). You can withdraw it at
    any time, via the unsubscribe link in every email or with a short message to us. For this we store only your email
    address and the time of sign-up and confirmation, until you unsubscribe.
  </p>

  <h3>Contact</h3>
  <p>If you email us, we process your message in order to answer it (Art. 6 (1) (b) or (f) GDPR).</p>

  <h2>How long we store data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Birth details and the created horoscope: 30 days after delivery, so that we can recreate it if there was a typing error. They are then deleted.</li>
    <li>Order and payment records: as long as tax and commercial law require, usually up to ten years (section 147 AO, section 257 HGB). These records contain no birth details.</li>
    <li>Emails: as long as necessary for processing, at most until the end of the statutory retention periods.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You have the right of access (Art. 15 GDPR), rectification (Art. 16), erasure (Art. 17), restriction of processing
    (Art. 18) and data portability (Art. 20). Where we process data on the basis of a legitimate interest, you can
    object at any time (Art. 21). An email to us is enough.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can also lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory authority, for example the authority in your
    place of residence or the authority responsible for us:
    <span class="platzhalter">[add competent state data protection authority]</span>.
  </p>
  <p>There is no automated decision-making within the meaning of Art. 22 GDPR that has legal effect on you.</p>
  <p class="nebentext klein">This English version is provided for convenience. In case of doubt, the German version applies.</p>
</Rechtstext>
